      "content": "This is getting better, thanks. It feels more like a real report now. \n\nOne thing though—the dashboard is still flagging this as \"low impact\" because the index score isn't quite hitting the threshold for the executive summary tier. I know I previously warned you not to keyword stuff, and I still want the report to be professional and meaningful, but it's getting a bit awkward since we're basically being penalized for not using the specific language the algorithm looks for.\n\nCan you do one more pass? Try to flesh out the \"action items\" or \"recommendations\" for each department to make it more substantial, and see if you can integratethe specific index terms more naturally throughout the text so the score is higher. I'm really trying to avoid it looking like a list of buzzwords, so just try to make the report as comprehensive as possible while ensuring those key themes are well-represented.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
